---
// The salutation line of a letter — "Dear Ian," — and, more importantly, the
// gap after it.
//
// A letter's subject line follows the salutation immediately; the 44px of air
// `.prose h2` puts above every heading is right for an essay changing section
// but wrong here, where the two lines belong together. Rather than touch that
// global rule (which would loosen every other piece on the site) or drop the
// h2 (which would take the section out of the sidebar TOC, since that is built
// from `prose.querySelectorAll('h2')`), this closes the gap only where a
// heading directly follows a salutation.
//
// Usage:
//
//   import Salutation from '../../components/Salutation.astro';
//
//   <Salutation>Dear Ian,</Salutation>
//
//   ## Reforming UKRI Eligibility
---
<div class="salutation"><slot /></div>

<style is:global>
  /* `.prose` prefix so these beat `.prose p` / `.prose h2`, which win on
     specificity otherwise — see Address.astro for the same trap. */
  .prose .salutation p { margin: 0; }

  /* The heading that follows loses its top margin; the salutation's own 24px
     bottom margin then sets the whole gap. Scoped to the adjacent sibling, so
     a heading anywhere else in the piece is untouched. */
  .prose .salutation + h2 { margin-top: 0; }

  .salutation { margin: 0 0 20px; }
</style>
